🤖 What is MCP?

MCP = Model Context Protocol

Think of an AI assistant as a smart student.

The AI knows many things, but sometimes it needs to use outside tools to do a job.

For example:

📁 Read a file
🔍 Search information
🗄️ Get data from a database
📧 Send an email
📊 Read Excel data
🌐 Access a website

MCP is like a common plug/socket that lets the AI connect to these tools.

🔌 Simple example

Imagine you have a robot 🤖.

The robot wants to:

"Read my Excel file and calculate the total."

The robot itself may not directly know how to open Excel.

MCP acts like a bridge:

AI Robot 🤖 → MCP → Excel Tool 📊 → Result → AI Robot

The AI says:

"Please give me the Excel data."

MCP connects the AI to the correct tool and brings the result back.

🏫 School example

Imagine a student named Ravi.

Ravi has different teachers:

| Teacher             | Helps with        |
| ------------------- | ----------------- |
| 📚 Maths teacher    | Calculations      |
| 🔬 Science teacher  | Science questions |
| 💻 Computer teacher | Computer work     |
| 📖 English teacher  | English           |


Ravi doesn't need to learn everything from every teacher.

He simply asks the right teacher.

Similarly:

AI = Ravi
MCP = Communication system
Tools = Teachers

⭐ One-line definition

MCP is a standard way for an AI to communicate with external tools and data.

